// orbit — a planet rolling inside a fixed ring with NO carrier, NO pins on
// the planet: the `tangent` mesh row is the entire joint. It enforces both
// pitch-circle contact and roll-without-slip, so a free gear, given only an
// initial position, orbits exactly as if an invisible carrier held it.
// Kinematically psi = -N_p/(N_r - N_p) * theta: this planet revolves once
// backwards for every four of its own turns.
//
//   mech run examples/orbit.mech
//
mechanism orbit {
  ground frame { anchor o at (0, 0) }
  gear gr { teeth: 40, module: 0.01 } on frame.o
  body pl { anchor c at (0.15, 0) }
  gear gp { teeth: 10, module: 0.01 } on pl.c
  mesh gp gr tangent
  drive pl at 60 deg/s
}
